## Abstract

One of the main goals of the STAR experiment is to study properties of the Quark-Gluon Plasma (QGP). An excellent probe of the QGP are charm quarks, as they are created in very early stages of the heavy-in collisions in the hard partonic scatterings. As a result, they experience the whole evolution of the hot and dense medium. The STAR experiment is able to access information about charm quark production via direct topological reconstruction of hadronic decays of the open-charm hadrons, utilizing the excellent pointing resolution of the Heavy Flavor Tracker detector. This thesis discusses the analysis of \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}\) meson production in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\mathrm{NN}}}=200\,\mathrm{GeV}\) collected by the STAR experiment in year 2016. The \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}\) mesons are reconstructed via their hadronic decay \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}\to\mathrm{K}^{\mp}\uppi^{\pm}\uppi^{\pm}\). The topological selection criteria are optimised using supervised machine learning techniques, utilizing the ROOT package TMVA. The measured 2016 invariant yield of \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}\) mesons is combined with that measured in year 2014 and subsequently used to calculate the nuclear modification factor, \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}/\mathrm{D}^{0}\) yield ratio, and total charm production cross section in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\mathrm{NN}}}=200\,\mathrm{GeV}\). The nuclear modification factor reveals significant suppression of high transverse momentum \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}\) mesons in 0-10% central Au+Au collisions, which indicates significant energy loss of charm quarks in the QGP. The measured \(\mathrm{D}^{\pm}/\mathrm{D}^{0}\) yield ratio appears to be consistent with PYTHIA calculation within the uncertainties. The total charm cross section per nucleon-nucleon collision in 10-40% Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\mathrm{NN}}}=200\,\mathrm{GeV}\) is found to be \(113.3\pm 6.2(\mathrm{stat})\pm 27.2(\mathrm{sys})\,\upmu\)b, consistent with the total cross section measured in p+p collisions at the same collision energy.

## Abstract

Jednim z hlavnich cilu experimentu STAR je studium vlastnosti kvark-gluonoveho plazmatu (QGP). Idealni sondou QGP jsou puvabne kvarky, protoze se tvori ve velmi rane fazi srazek tezkych jader, v tvrdych partonovych srazkach. To znamena, ze jsou pfitomny po celou dobu evoluce QGP. V experimentu STAR je mozne merit produkci puvabnych kvarku prostrednictvim prime topologicke rekonstrukce hadronovych rozpadu hadronu s otevenym puvabem, pomoci velmi presneho prostoveho rozlisenf delektoru Heavy Flavor Tracker. Tato prace obsahuje detailni popis analyzy produkce mezonu D\({}^{\pm}\) ve srazkach Au+Au pri energii \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=200\,\)GeV, namerenych experimentem STAR v roce 2016. Mezony D\({}^{\pm}\) jsou rekonstruovany prostrednictvim jejich hadronoveho rozpadoveho kanalu D\({}^{\pm}\to{\rm K}^{\mp}\pi^{\pm}\pi^{\pm}\). Topologicka vyberova kriteria jsou optimalizovana pomoci strojoveho uenen s pomoci ROOT balicku TMVA. Invariantni vtytezek D\({}^{\pm}\) mezonu namereny v datech z roku 2016 je skombinovan s merenim z roku 2014 a nasledne pouzit pri vypoctu jaderneho modifikacnrho faktoru, pomeru vtytezku D\({}^{\pm}\)/D\({}^{0}\) a celkoveho ucinneho prurezu produkce puvabnych kvarku ve srazkach Au+Au pri energii \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=200\,\)GeV. Z mereni jaderneho modifikacnrho faktoru je patrme signifikantni potlaceni produkce D\({}^{\pm}\) mezonu s velkou priconu hybnosti ve srazkach Au+Au s centralitou 0-10%, ktere je pravdepodobne zpusobeno energetickymi ztratami puvabnych kvarku v QGP. Pomer vytezku D\({}^{\pm}\)/D\({}^{0}\) se v ramci chy mereni nelsi od teoretickcho vypoctu tohoto pomeru pomoci PYTHIA. Celkovy ucinny prurez produkce puvabnych kvarku ve srazkach Au+Au pri energii \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=200\,\)GeV s centralitou 10-40% byl zmeren s hodnotou \(113.3\pm 6.2({\rm stat})\pm 27.2({\rm sys})\) u, ktera souhlasi s hodnotou zmerenou ve srazkach p+p pri stejne energii.

