mainly from hadronization of the QGP bulk. It is also interesting and important to study collective flow of heavy quarks, which can be accessed by measurement of open heavy-flavor hadrons. The origin of collective flow for heavy flavor hadrons is slightly different than for light hadrons, as heavy quarks originate exclusively from the hard partonic scattering and therefore do not have any information about the collective motion of the medium in early stage of the collision. The details about collective flow of open-charm hadrons will be discussed in the following chapter.

Another important thing to discuss is that collective flow is not a phenomenon observed in heavy-in collisions only. Not that long ago, it was generally accepted, that harmonic flow is a medium induced effect and should be observable exclusively in ultra-relativistic heavy-ions collisions. With development of more sophisticated experimental techniques and increased collision energies at the LHC, it was discovered, that collective

