#### 4.2.3 Total reconstruction efficiency

The total D\({}^{\pm}\) meson reconstruction efficiency is first determined separately for the \(st\_physics\) and \(st\_sst+st\_nosst\) streams using:

\[\varepsilon(p_{\rm T})=\varepsilon_{\rm HFT+TPC}(p_{\rm T})\varepsilon_{\rm PID} (p_{\rm T}). \tag{4.6}\]

The efficiencies for the two subsets are then combined as a weighted average, where the weights are numbers of good events in the \(st\_physics\) and \(st\_sst+st\_nosst\) streams.

