All results presented in this summary are from Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=200\) GeV which were collected by the STAR experiment in years 2014 and 2016. Topological reconstruction of the decays, using an excellent vertex position resolution from the Heavy-Flavor Tracker (HFT) [8], was used to extract the signals of the open-charm hadrons listed in Table 1.

