## 3 Results

Figure 4 shows the nuclear modification factor \(R_{\mathrm{AA}}\) of \(\mathrm{D^{0}}\)[15] and \(\mathrm{D^{\pm}}\) mesons as a function of \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) in 0%-10% central Au+Au collisions. Both \(\mathrm{D^{0}}\) and \(\mathrm{D^{\pm}}\) are significantly suppressed in high-\(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) region which suggests a significant energy loss of charm quarks in the QGP. The low to intermediate \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) bump structure is consistent with predictions of models incorporating large collective flow of charm quarks [15].

